                <pb facs="0694" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg558"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./442:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cook</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-25T15:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1929—3
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. If you perceive no objection please ask the Venezuelan Government to continue
                    the temporary operating permit of Pan American <pb facs="0695" n="559"
                        xml:id="pg559"/> Airways, Incorporated, pending the conclusion of the formal
                    contract and to have the Venezuelan Post Office accept at Maracay mail
                    despatched by the United States Post Office, as requested in the latter’s
                    cablegram of May 4 to the Venezuelan Postal Administration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
